        "faq_item_9QefQB": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is Dr. Jen's toothpaste safe to use?",
            "answer": "<p>Dr. Jen's KeraHAp™ is the first Peptide + Nano-hydroxyapatite toothpaste, trusted by dental professionals nationwide. Dr. Jen has spent six years perfecting these advanced formulations, sourcing the highest-grade Nano-hydroxyapatite available. Our rod-shaped crystals meet rigorous EU safety standards for synthetic nHAp. While other brands have approached us wanting to use our premium sources, we protect the integrity of our supply chain to ensure every tube meets our exacting standards. Current studies show that Nano-hydroxyapatite using rod-shaped crystals is safe to use in toothpaste. Link to study</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_X9HyFN": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Which formula is right for me?",
            "answer": "<p>Dr. Jen's KeraHAp™ combines 10% premium Nano-hydroxyapatite with advanced enamel-inspired peptides for biomimetic enamel support. It is the most advanced fluoride-free formula in the Dr. Jen's lineup, designed for patients who want the highest level of enamel support available.<br/><br/>Dr. Jen's Super Paste combines 10% premium Nano-hydroxyapatite with fluoride and xylitol, clinically proven to outperform fluoride-only toothpastes. Available in Mint and Strawberry.<br/><br/>Dr. Jen's Fluoride-Free delivers proven enamel support without fluoride, powered by 10% premium Nano-hydroxyapatite and a proprietary essential oil complex. Available in Mint and Strawberry.<br/><br/>Dr. Jen's Eggshell is the first and only eggshell-derived nHAp toothpaste, formulated with 10% premium eggshell Nano-hydroxyapatite. Eggshells contain magnesium and zinc, which promote higher mineral uptake for enhanced enamel protection. Available in Mint and Orange Mango.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_HQ84kE": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is Nano-hydroxyapatite?",
            "answer": "<p>Nano-hydroxyapatite (nHAp) is a biocompatible mineral that mirrors the structure of your tooth enamel. The \"nano\" means the particles are extremely small, measured in nanometers, allowing them to behave like your enamel crystals.</p><p><strong>How it works:</strong></p><ul><li>Absorbs and removes dental plaque</li><li>Replenishes lost calcium and phosphate minerals</li><li>Fills in micro-fissures on tooth surfaces</li><li>Reduces sensitivity by sealing exposed dentinal tubules</li></ul><p>Think of it as giving your teeth the building blocks they need to stay strong.<br/><br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_mFfdaE": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why does Dr. Jen's cost more than other toothpastes?",
            "answer": "<p>There's something we want you to know because behind every tube is a story that started long before it reached your bathroom shelf.<br/>It began in a hospital room.<br/><br/>Years ago, Dr. Jen's daughter became dangerously ill with a life-threatening stomach condition. As any parent would, Dr. Jen searched for every way to support her daughter's healing, down to the smallest details, including something as simple as toothpaste.<br/>What she discovered shocked her.<br/>Fluoride-free toothpastes aren't regulated. Brands can claim \"Nanohydroxyapatite\" while using cheap, low-quality versions or including so little that it does almost nothing. Labels didn't tell the full truth, and Dr. Jen couldn't find a single toothpaste that matched what the science said her daughter needed.<br/><br/>In that hospital room, one thing became clear: <strong>if the right toothpaste didn't exist, she would have to create it.</strong><br/><br/>A mother's worry became a mission.<br/>Dr. Jen spent years studying particle size, purity, concentration, safety, and biocompatibility. She rejected anything that didn't meet the highest standard, even when it cost more.<br/>Only true high-grade Nanohydroxyapatite Only the optimal concentration proven to protect enamel Only clean, gut-friendly ingredients gentle enough for someone fighting for their health<br/>No shortcuts. No compromises. Just a formula built with the same care she wanted for her own child.<br/>That's why our toothpaste costs more. Because it was never created to be the cheapest. It was created to be the safest, the purest, and the most effective. Born from fear, love, science, and the determination of a mother who refused to settle.<br/><br/><strong>And yet, it comes down to 25 cents a day.</strong><br/>For up to 25 cents per day, you give your enamel the level of protection research actually supports, without the gut-disrupting ingredients found in many conventional formulas. About the same as your morning coffee, but for your long-term health.<br/><a href=\"https://www.mdpi.com/1660-4601/19/9/5629\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"https://www.mdpi.com/1660-4601/19/9/5629\"><strong><br/>Link Study </strong></a><br/>Nanohydroxyapatite (nHAp) in the Remineralization <br/>of Early Dental Caries: A Scoping Review.<br/>Published in May 2022. PMID: 35565022</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_MEG9f3": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I use Dr. Jen's toothpaste?",
            "answer": "<p>Brush as you normally would, then spit out the excess but don't rinse. For maximum mineral uptake, wait 30 minutes before eating or drinking. This allows the Nano-hydroxyapatite to fully bond with your enamel. As always, discuss any specific questions or concerns with your dental team, who knows your personal oral health best.</p>"
